{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Face to face, YHWH spoke with you.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): without an intermediary, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 33:11): ״כאשר ידבר איש אל רעהו״ — as a man speaks to his fellow — that there is no intermediary between them." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'Face to face' — in many likenesses was the Holy One, blessed be He, likened to Israel: to this one He appeared standing and to that one sitting, to this one as a young man and to that one as an old man, as it is said (Hosea 12:11): ״וביד הנביאים אדמה״ — 'and by the hand of the prophets I am likened.' At the Sea of Reeds, as a young man arrayed for battle, as it is said (Exodus 15:3): ״ה׳ איש מלחמה״ — YHWH is a man of war. At Mount Sinai, as an old man sitting in the academy, for there is no Torah except from the mouth of an elder, as it is said (Psalms 119): ״מזקנים אתבונן״ — 'from the elders I gain understanding.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'face to face' — I have already explained in the section of Ki Tissa."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:47.729903771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}